    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0954" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">683.84A/4–1452: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 420<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Syria (Cannon) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d420-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-04-14T16:00:00+02:00">April 14, 1952—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>585. Department pass Defense. Thanks Major Jaddid’s cooperation attitude MAC chairman Col. Taxis
                    obtained Syrian consent in January Israel closing Jordan River sluice gates in
                    order repair Daughter Jacob’s Bridge
                        (Legtel 462, February 6). Israeli have
                    made little effort repair bridge, but have taken advantage opportunity work
                    intensively on drainage project when weather permitted.</p>
                <p>Now that water level receding Syrians state floodgates must be opened permit
                    continued irrigation valuable crops Bouteiha farm and last week asked Taxis relay request. Israeli refused, stating
                    Syrians had no say on affairs in zone which is “under Israel sovereignty”.
                    Syrians aroused by Israel intransigence and there were some mutterings they
                    would take action open floodgates if Taxis unable do so.</p>
                <p>In emergency meeting with Israel chairman April 12 we understand Taxis succeeded in obtaining his agreement open
                    gates provided Taxis would seek consent
                    Syrians allow closing gates few hours daily for short period permit completion
                    repairs bridge. While Jaddid and owners
                    Bouteiha farm probably would agree <pb facs="0955" n="915" xml:id="pg915"/> such
                    arrangement, they are convinced Israeli using bridge repairs only as pretext
                    pursue drainage project. Situation thus continues potentially dangerous and
                    military attaché and Legation officer planning early visit zone observe
                    developments.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi> Most unsettling factor continues be Israeli
                    reiteration claim of sovereignty over zone and denial Syrian demands discuss in
                        MAC affairs within zone affecting Arabs
                    including drainage project which also affects property owners in Syria (Legtel 319, December 4 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >3</hi>]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d420-f2"/>). Israel continued non-compliance
                    important provisions May 18, 1951 SC resolution
                    is factor striking root Syrian confidence in UN
                    and west which in other fields has been improving.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Cannon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
